<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-CSR reviews timber business.</title>
<headline>RTRS-CSR reviews timber business.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Building materials, aluminium and sugar group CSR Ltd said on Friday it had engaged investment bankers Credit Suisse First Boston to assist in evaluating options for the restructure of the group's timber operations.</p>
<p>CSR said that since November it had implemented a two-year improvement plan in its timber division, which was expected to significantly improve the operational performance of the business and the value to shareholders.</p>
<p>It said the plans aimed to reduce operating and distribution costs. But it added that a large number of alternative options for the timber business needed to be assessed.  </p>
<p>&quot;This process is expected to take some time to be completed and no decisions have yet been made on any specific option,&quot; CSR said.</p>
<p>CSR's timber business has a turnover of about A$700 million a year.</p>
<p>CSR shares closed four cents lower at A$4.38.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
